---
// How evalsets pair real and fake: same corpus against cross corpus.
import { FG } from "../../lib/figures";
---

<figure class="fig">
            <div style="border: 1px solid var(--rule); background: var(--card); padding: 20px; display: grid; grid-template-columns: var(--f-two); gap: 28px 32px; min-width: 0">
              <div style="display: grid; gap: 10px; align-content: start; min-width: 0">
                <div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 6px 10px"><code style="font: 500 12px/1 var(--mono); padding: 5px 7px; background: var(--ink); color: var(--paper)">same_corpus</code><span style="font-size: 0.86rem; color: var(--muted)">feeds headline numbers</span></div>
                <div style="border: 1px solid var(--ink); background: var(--paper); padding: 10px 12px; display: grid; gap: 3px; text-align: center; font-size: 0.86rem; line-height: 1.4"><span style="font: 500 11.5px/1.4 var(--mono); color: var(--muted)">one corpus</span>The same speakers, microphones and rooms on both sides</div>
                <div aria-hidden="true" style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; text-align: center; font: 500 15px/1 var(--mono); color: var(--muted)"><span>↓</span><span>↓</span></div>
                <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 10px">
                  <div style="border: 1px solid var(--rule); padding: 8px 10px; display: grid; gap: 6px; min-width: 0">
                    <div aria-hidden="true" style="height: 30px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 2px">{FG.pw.sameR.map((b) => (<Fragment><span style={`flex: 1 1 0; height: ${b.h}; background: var(--stone)`}></span></Fragment>))}</div>
                    <span style="font-size: 0.84rem; line-height: 1.35"><b style="font-weight: 600">Real</b>, as recorded</span>
                  </div>
                  <div style="border: 1px solid var(--rule); padding: 8px 10px; display: grid; gap: 6px; min-width: 0">
                    <div aria-hidden="true" style="height: 30px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 2px">{FG.pw.sameF.map((b) => (<Fragment><span style={`flex: 1 1 0; height: ${b.h}; background: var(--accent)`}></span></Fragment>))}</div>
                    <span style="font-size: 0.84rem; line-height: 1.35"><b style="font-weight: 600">Fake</b>, made from the same speakers</span>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.45">Only the synthesis differs, so a high AUC means the detector found it.</p>
              </div>
              <div style="display: grid; gap: 10px; align-content: start; min-width: 0">
                <div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 6px 10px"><code style="font: 500 12px/1 var(--mono); padding: 4px 6px; background: var(--tint); color: var(--ink); border: 1px solid var(--rule-2)">cross_corpus</code><span style="font-size: 0.86rem; color: var(--muted)">never averaged into headlines</span></div>
                <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 10px">
                  <div style="border: 1px solid var(--ink); background: var(--paper); padding: 10px 12px; display: grid; gap: 3px; text-align: center; font-size: 0.86rem; line-height: 1.4"><span style="font: 500 11.5px/1.4 var(--mono); color: var(--muted)">corpus A</span>Real speech from one source</div>
                  <div style="border: 1px solid var(--ink); background: var(--paper); padding: 10px 12px; display: grid; gap: 3px; text-align: center; font-size: 0.86rem; line-height: 1.4"><span style="font: 500 11.5px/1.4 var(--mono); color: var(--muted)">corpus B</span>Fakes from another</div>
                </div>
                <div aria-hidden="true" style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; text-align: center; font: 500 15px/1 var(--mono); color: var(--muted)"><span>↓</span><span>↓</span></div>
                <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 10px">
                  <div style="border: 1px solid var(--rule); padding: 8px 10px; display: grid; gap: 6px; min-width: 0">
                    <div aria-hidden="true" style="height: 30px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 2px">{FG.pw.crossR.map((b) => (<Fragment><span style={`flex: 1 1 0; height: ${b.h}; background: var(--stone)`}></span></Fragment>))}</div>
                    <span style="font-size: 0.84rem; line-height: 1.35"><b style="font-weight: 600">Real</b>, quiet room, one microphone</span>
                  </div>
                  <div style="border: 1px solid var(--rule); padding: 8px 10px; display: grid; gap: 6px; min-width: 0">
                    <div aria-hidden="true" style="height: 30px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 2px">{FG.pw.crossF.map((b) => (<Fragment><span style={`flex: 1 1 0; height: ${b.h}; background: var(--accent)`}></span></Fragment>))}</div>
                    <span style="font-size: 0.84rem; line-height: 1.35"><b style="font-weight: 600">Fake</b>, louder, another sample rate</span>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 6px"><span style="font-size: 0.84rem; color: var(--muted)">Also differs:</span><span style="font: 400 11.5px/1 var(--mono); padding: 4px 6px; border: 1px dashed var(--rule-3)">microphone</span><span style="font: 400 11.5px/1 var(--mono); padding: 4px 6px; border: 1px dashed var(--rule-3)">noise</span><span style="font: 400 11.5px/1 var(--mono); padding: 4px 6px; border: 1px dashed var(--rule-3)">loudness</span><span style="font: 400 11.5px/1 var(--mono); padding: 4px 6px; border: 1px dashed var(--rule-3)">sample rate</span></div>
                <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.45">A detector can score well by telling the corpora apart. Each cross-corpus set gets a shortcut probe.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <figcaption><strong>Two ways to pair real and fake.</strong> Every result row carries its pairing. A cross-corpus example: <code>mlaad_si</code> pairs MLAAD's Sinhala fakes with OpenSLR's real Sinhala speech.</figcaption>
          </figure>
